chemical industry. The reason? Production is centralized and fossil fuel-dependent. The
solution? Localized production using an undervalued resource: biogas. The US produces enough
biogas to make over $20 bn/y worth of chemicals, but 60% is wasted in low-margin applications or
flared altogether.

